{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787774751,"nonce":"ehOuT0hAfP6cGlHsMkcqoG9Tklo=","title":"fix(k8s): /workspace ownership is the step's contract — services get membership, never ownership (908f534)","message":"\u003e Imported from pull request #110 (MERGED)\n\u003e Branch: `fix/908f534-fsgroup-workspace` → `main`\n\u003e Created: 2026-08-26T15:14:27Z · Merged: 2026-08-26T15:24:38Z\n\nCloses git-bug 908f534. Merge after #106 (warm_eviction compile fix).\n\nA step with `needs:` AND a sidecar service pinning a non-root uid got a /workspace chowned to the SERVICE's gid (root:999) — the fetcher (uid 65532) couldn't write and the step was refused its workspace before it started. The preferred fix (CSI delivery, fsGroupPolicy: None) died with ADR-0066/0067, so this arbitrates directly: workspace Pods ALWAYS keep `fsGroup = WORKSPACE_GID`; a service's pinned gid rides Pod `supplementalGroups` instead.\n\nThe inversion is safe because the original rationale (10f4c82: \"the service's data emptyDir needs group-write\") is vacuous in the sidecar topology — `service_sidecar` mounts ZERO volumes; postgres PGDATA lives in the image's writable layer, which fsGroup never touched. Standalone shared-service Pods unchanged. Review verified every pod shape old→new: the only shape losing an fsGroup (non-workspace step + service) loses nothing real (Secret mounts are 0644; the sidecar's gid still rides supplementalGroups).\n\nTests: the exact broken combo (needs: + non-root service → fsGroup 65532 + supplemental [65532,999]) plus the two inverted assertions renamed to the new contract. Suite: 954/954.\n\n**Live proof still owed** (the \"reports success but structurally cannot work\" class): a pipeline with a producer step + a needs: step declaring `run_as_user: 999` postgres that writes /workspace — deferred to the e2e pass, noted in the ticket on close.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":null}]}